Part 1: Core Logic Architecture
1. The "Anchor-First" Prompt Formula
Research into V7 confirms a phenomenon called Token Attention Decay. The model prioritizes the first 5–10 words. The previous formula (Scene + Style + Context) is mechanically flawed because it buries the cinematic context at the end.
The New Generation Rule: The AI Agent must assemble the final prompt string in this exact inverted order:
[Cinematic Context] + [Subject & Action] + [Visual Style & Lighting] + [Technical Specs] + [Parameters]
Component Definitions:
1. [Cinematic Context] (The Anchor): Hard-coded string. Format: Cinematic shot from the movie [Movie Title] ([Year]) directed by [Director Name].
2. [Subject & Action]: User-selected scene description.
3. [Visual Style & Lighting]: Aesthetic modifiers and geometric lighting (e.g., "Volumetric beams").
4. [Technical Specs] (The Fix for No SREF): Specific hardware triggers (e.g., "Shot on Kodak Vision3 500T," "Anamorphic lens").
5. [Parameters]: --ar 2.39:1 --v 7 --style raw (Mandatory for photorealism).

