Part 4: Exhaustive Feature Guide (Text-Only Focus)
Midjourney V7 offers several powerful features that function purely via text parameters, perfect for your app's current limitations.
1. Batch Runs & Permutations ({})
Since you cannot iterate via image upload, use Permutations to batch-test text variables. This allows the user to generate multiple variations of a prompt in a single request.
• Syntax: Enclose comma-separated options in curly braces {}.
• App Feature: Create a "Compare Lenses" button that injects {35mm lens, 85mm lens, Fisheye lens} into the [Technical Specs] slot.
• Result: Midjourney will run 3 separate jobs: one for 35mm, one for 85mm, etc.
• Limit: Fast Mode only (Maximum 40 jobs for Pro users).
2. Repeat (--repeat)
Use this to brute-force a "lucky seed." V7's output is deterministic based on the seed, but the initial seed is random.
• Syntax: Add --repeat [Number] to the end.
• App Feature: "Burst Mode." Adds --repeat 5 to the prompt.
• Why: Essential for action shots (e.g., John Wick club scene) where the random placement of smoke/lasers makes or breaks the image. Running it 5 times guarantees at least one good composition.
3. Negative Prompting (--no)
This instructs the model on what not to render.
• Syntax: --no [item1], [item2]
• Logic: This is mathematically equivalent to weighing a concept at ::-0.5.
• Constraint: Do not use sentences like "no red cars." The model may see "red car" and generate it. Use list format: --no red cars.
• App Feature: "Clean Up" toggle. Injects: --no text, watermark, signature, blur, distortion.
4. Multi-Prompting & Weights (::)
Use this to separate concepts that are "bleeding" into each other.
• Syntax: [Concept A]::[Weight] [Concept B]::[Weight]
• Problem: "Hot Dog" -> Generates a frankfurter.
• Fix: Hot:: Dog:: -> Generates a dog that is hot.
• App Feature: Slider for "Atmosphere Strength."
    ◦ Low: [Scene]::1 [Foggy Atmosphere]::0.5
    ◦ High: [Scene]::1 [Foggy Atmosphere]::2
5. Draft Mode (--draft)
This is the economic engine for V7.
• Syntax: --draft
• Benefit: Runs at ~10x speed and consumes ~50% of the GPU minutes.
• Strategy: Your app should default to --draft for the first generation to allow users to "preview" the composition. Once they like a result, they can re-run the exact same prompt and seed without --draft to get the full V7 quality.

