Part 5: Future Integration (When SREF Works)
When your app gains the ability to pass Image URLs, implement this section immediately. This is the "Holy Grail" of style consistency.
1. Style Reference (--sref)
• Function: Replaces the need for complex style descriptions.
• Implementation: [Prompt] --sref [URL]
• Visual Style Weight (--sw): Controls how strong the reference is.
    ◦ --sw 100 (Default)
    ◦ --sw 1000 (Max - overrides text prompt style completely).
2. Omni Reference (--oref)
• Function: Replaces "Character Reference" (--cref). It locks the identity of a person or an object.
• Implementation: [Prompt] --oref [URL]
• Omni Weight (--ow):
    ◦ --ow 10 (Style transfer only).
    ◦ --ow 1000 (Strict pixel-perfect structure retention).
3. SREF Codes (The "Text-Only" Bridge)
• Tip: You don't actually need to host images to use SREF now. Midjourney supports "SREF Codes" (random seeds that act as styles).
• Hack: You can hard-code specific "Vibes" using these random numbers.
